tion:¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ$So shall they be life unto thy soul,¦layout ‚¤text¶And grace to thy neck.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ'Then shalt thou walk in thy way safely,¦layout ‚¤text¿And thy foot shall not stumble.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ/When thou liest down, thou shalt not be afraid:¦layout ‚¤textÙ7Yea, thou shalt lie down, and thy sleep shall be sweet.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text½Be not afraid of sudden fear,¦layout ‚¤textÙ8Neither of the desolation of the wicked, when it cometh.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ%For the LORD shall be thy confidence,¦layout ‚¤textÙ)And shall keep thy foot from being taken.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ.Withhold not good from them to whom it is due,¦layout ‚¤textÙ/When it is in the power of thine hand to do it.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ/Say not unto thy neighbour, Go, and come again,¦layout ‚¤textÙ5And to morrow I will give; when thou hast it by thee.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ&Devise not evil against thy neighbour,¦layout ‚¤textÙ$Seeing he dwelleth securely by thee.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ$Strive not with a man without cause,¦layout ‚¤text½If he have done thee no harm.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse#¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤text¼Envy thou not the oppressor,¦layout ‚¤text¼And choose none of his ways.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ+For the froward is abomination to the LORD:¦layout ‚¤textÙ%But his secret is with the righteous.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ4The curse of the LORD is in the house of the wicked:¦layout ‚¤